    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0010" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg4"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.24/42: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Scott</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-06-28T17:00:00-04:30">June 28, 1939—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:16 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. Department’s instruction of June 27, 7 p.m. The Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    states that his Government cannot express an opinion until it has had time to
                    study the exact copy of the proposed legislation. If the Department will kindly
                    forward same by air mail I will endeavor to obtain an expression of opinion as
                    quickly as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Scott</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
